From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH v4] comctl32/toolbar: Lay out TB_SETROWS by separator groups in vertical wrapable toolbars.

AI-assisted (Claude), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted
upstream. v1 is the Inventor patch from Autodesk-Inventor-for-Linux
eddb691 (wine-11.19-1).

Windows 10 (own MEASURE, comctl32 5.82 and 6.16, x86_64 and i686,
2026-11-10): in a CCS_VERT | TBSTYLE_WRAPABLE toolbar, TB_SETROWS starts
every group of buttons between separators on a new row and gives each
separator a row of its own; the number of buttons per row is the one that
gives the most button rows not above the request, or with bLarger the
fewest that reach it, separators not counted (47 buttons in 5 groups,
TB_SETROWS(12): 5 per row). The rows stay when buttons are replaced and
when the toolbar is sized to the returned rectangle; after a change of
its width it has as many buttons per row as fit into the new width,
still with the groups and separator rows.

Wine set the wrap points and wrapped again by the window's width inside
TB_SETROWS, so a vertical toolbar came back with one column; Inventor
sizes its drawing-text symbol palette to that rectangle.

v2 (2026-11-08) handled bLarger (Wine's tbrows_results table).

v3 (2026-11-10, after the measurement): the group rule only for vertical
wrapable toolbars; other toolbars keep Wine's code, which v2 had changed
(46 measured horizontal cases that Wine already did like Windows came out
wrong). The rows are kept until the toolbar's width changes, no longer
for good (Windows re-wraps after a resize); TB_SETROWS' own resize does
not count. New test test_setrows_groups with the measured vertical cases
(left out: rows Windows does not return from, and the 3+4 groups with 4
rows, where Windows' choice does not follow the rule) and the horizontal
cases Wine handles like Windows, run for comctl32 5 and 6.

v4 (2026-11-10, after the maintainer's L4 in Inventor 2027): with v3 the
palette fell apart - Inventor changes the toolbar's width after
TB_SETROWS, and v3 handed it to Wine's width wrap, which puts the
separators inside rows. Windows (same measurement, palette sequence)
keeps the groups and separator rows after a width change and fits
width / button width buttons per row (500 pixels: one row per group;
60 pixels: 2 per row with its 23-pixel buttons). v4 does that in
TOOLBAR_Size. New test test_setrows_palette with the measured sequence;
the 60-pixel step is todo_wine, Wine's buttons being 16 pixels wide there
(button size with TB_SETPADDING(0, 0) and no strings, outside this patch).

